      "answer": "$-2<x<0$ and $0<x<2$",
      "official_mark_scheme_text": "$\\frac{dy}{dx}=-\\frac{12}{x^4}+\\frac3{x^2}$. B1.\nSet derivative $=0$ or use $<,\\le$ and simplify: $-\\frac{12}{x^4}+\\frac3{x^2}=0$ leading to $3x^4-12x^2=0$ or $-12+3x^2=0$. M1. Must be from $\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{A}{x^4}+\\frac{B}{x^2}$.\n$3x^2(x^2-4)=0$ leading to $x=\\pm2$ only. A1. SC B1 for $x=\\pm2$ if M0 scored.\n$-2<x<0$ and $0<x<2$, or $(-2,0)$ and $(0,2)$, or $-2<x<2$ and $x\\neq0$. B1 FT B1 FT. Allow and/or. Allow $-2\\le x<0$ and/or $0<x\\le2$ but only B1B0 if 0 included. Allow $[-2,0)$ and $(0,2]$. Allow B1B0 for $-2<x<2$ or $(-2,2)$. Must be B1B1 from derivative form.\nTotal: 5",
