      "answer": "$6.51$",
      "official_mark_scheme_text": "At $x=1$, $y=3$ and $m_{\\mathrm{tan}}=-9$. *M1. Using their $\\frac{dy}{dx}$.\n$m_{norm}=-\\frac1{-9}=\\frac19$. DM1.\nEquation of normal is $y-3=\\frac19(x-1)$, leading to $y=\\frac19x+\\frac{26}{9}$. A1.\nAt $x=-1$, $y=1$, $m=-9$. M1.\nEquation of tangent is $y-1=-9(x+1)$, leading to $y=-9x-8$. A1.\nMeet when $\\frac19x+\\frac{26}{9}=-9x-8$, leading to $x=-1.19512\\ldots=-\\frac{49}{41}$. M1. Equates their tangent and their normal.\nArea $=\\frac12\\times$ their $1.19512\\ldots\\times$ their $(\\frac{26}{9}+8)$. M1. If $\\int y_2-y_1$ is used integration must be correct and substitution shown.\n$6.51$. A1 AWRT. Accept fraction written as 6.51.\nTotal: 8",
